4. Likewise; in like manner; in the same way.

{{smaller block|As God clothes himself with light as with a garment, so God clothes and apparels his works with light ''too.''
{{right|''Donne,'' Sermons, vi.}}}}

{{smaller block|Lewis the Fourteenth in his old age became religious: he determined that his subjects should be religious ''too.''
{{right|''Macaulay,'' Leigh Hunt.}}}}

'''Too blame.''' See ''blame, v. t.,'' note.—'''Too many.''' See ''many''<sup>1</sup>.—'''Too much for one.''' See ''much.''—'''Too thin.''' See ''thin''<sup>1</sup>.—'''Too too.''' (''a'') Quite too; altogether too: noting great excess or intensity, and formerly so much affected as to be regarded as one word, and so often written with a hyphen.

{{smaller block|O, that this ''too too'' solid flesh would melt,
Thaw, and resolve itself into a dew!
{{right|''Shak.,'' Hamlet, i. 2. 129.}}}}

{{smaller block|O ''too-too'' happy! had that Fall of thine
Not cancell'd so the Character diuine.
{{right|''Sylvester,'' tr. of Du Bartas's Weeks, i. 6.}}}}

{{smaller block|Their loues they on the tenter-hookes did racke,
Rost, boyl'd, bak'd, ''too too'' much white, claret, sacke.
{{right|''John Taylor,'' Pennilesse Pilgrimage, quoted in N. and Q.,}}
{{right|[7th ser., X. 498.}}}}

{{smaller block|The rigour and extremity of law
Is sometimes ''too-too'' bitter.
{{right|''Ford,'' Perkin Warbeck, ii. 2.}}}}

Hence—(''b''†) As an adjective or an adverb, very good; very well: used absolutely. ''Ray,'' English Words (ed. 1691), p. 76. (''c'') As an adjective, superlative; extreme; utter; hence, enraptured; gushing: applied to the so-called esthetic school, their principles, etc., in allusion to their exaggerated affectation. See ''estheticism,'' 2. [Colloq.]

{{smaller block|Let the exclusive ''too-too'' æsthetes tolerate the remark that music and painting do not exist for them, or even for the real masters in their respective arts, but for their power of addressing, influencing, and delighting the masses of mankind.
{{right|''N. and Q.,'' 7th ser., XI. 30.}}}}

